1943. Along with two other crew members, Zamperini survived the crash and spent 47 days adrift in a life raft, battling starvation, dehydration, and shark attacks. After drifting over 2,000 miles, Zamperini and his surviving companion, Russell Phillips, were captured by the Japanese navy. Zamperini was taken as a prisoner of war and held in several Japanese prison camps where he endured brutal treatment, starvation, and physical and psychological torture for over two years until he was finally released. Zamperini’s biography “Unbroken: A World War II Story of Survival, Resilience, and Redemption” was published in 2010 and was adapted into a Hollywood film directed by Angelina Jolie in 2014.","LocalizedString":"Louis Zamperini's story during WWII is a tale of survival and resilience. He was an Olympic athlete that turned bombardier of the United States Army Air Force, but his aircraft crashed in the Pacific Ocean during a rescue mission in 1943. Along with two other crew members, Zamperini survived the crash and spent 47 days adrift in a life raft, battling starvation, dehydration, and shark attacks. After drifting over 2,000 miles, Zamperini and his surviving companion, Russell Phillips, were captured by the Japanese navy. Zamperini was taken as a prisoner of war and held in several Japanese prison camps where he endured brutal treatment, starvation, and physical and psychological torture for over two years until he was finally released. Zamperini’s biography “Unbroken: A World War II Story of Survival, Resilience, and Redemption” was published in 2010 and was adapted into a Hollywood film directed by Angelina Jolie in 2014."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Suppress"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Fi